{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Epic progress + handoff (session cluttered-psychotic-leonberger, b97a-aebc-2bf0-47f2)\n\n**3 of 6 stories done. Epic must NOT be closed yet.**\n\n| story | state | change |\n|---|---|---|\n| 35bc finicky-rainbowy-weevil | **closed** | 969 MERGED (`23e51a014`) |\n| 0a8c horrendous-undivining-mare | **closed** | 971 MERGED (`87478f047`) |\n| 2aa6 tourmaline-anthracite-robberfly | in_progress, work complete | 977 `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified` pending |\n| 93d0, 44c7 | open — unblock when 2aa6 closes | — |\n| 5f4d | open — last, depends on all | — |\n\nThe external blocker **1f32** (flinty-unwhite-wolf) was verified fixed (merged as\n`095c4afef`, ADR 0053 grandfathering live) and closed on the original session's behalf with\noperator approval; that is what unblocked this chain.\n\n**Store migration is DONE:** 106 tickets migrated off `## Success Criteria`. Zero tickets\nnow carry the heading; the 8 remaining string matches are backticked prose in this epic's\nown tickets. Restore files: `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar-sc-migration-restore-2026-07-25.json`\n(+ `-stragglers.json`).\n\n### Two things the next agent MUST resolve before closing this epic\n\n**1. The epic's own AC1 conflicts with 2aa6's deliberate exclusions.** Epic AC1 requires no\nlive file under `src/rebar/` to match SC vocabulary, granting exclusions only for frozen\nfixtures, the vendor bundle and `O-RAN-SC`. But three live files legitimately retain the\nstring and 2aa6's AC6 *requires* one of them to:\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_T2.md` — \"a pilot with metrics, or stated success\n  criteria for a trial\": generic English about whether an experiment succeeded.\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_verifier.md` and `..._agentic.md` — the\n  `dod_uncertifiable` \"definition-of-done / success criterion\" wording, which this epic's\n  own Scope defers as a separate concept.\nEpic AC1 needs those three carve-outs added, or the epic cannot honestly close. The\nplan-review bot flagged this as advisory on 2aa6.\n\n**2. This epic's plans repeatedly wrote blanket string prohibitions that collide with their\nown exclusions.** Three so far — 35bc AC1/AC3, 2aa6 AC1, 2aa6 AC3 — each needed amending\nmid-implementation, each costing a re-review. **5f4d is very likely to hit the same thing**,\nsince its entire job is a CI guard plus an allowlist of exactly these exclusions. Its guard\nmust allowlist `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_criteria_heading_collapse.py` (already noted\non 5f4d) and the three files above.\n\n**Also note:** this epic's attestation is **stale** — amending 35bc's and 2aa6's descriptions\nbroke its `plan-material-pin` for those children. A fresh `rebar review-plan` is required\nbefore any close attempt."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785018384966894001,"uuid":"afe3b7fc-e3fd-439f-9a3f-0e66f4567a2f"}